tive","not evaluated"]]},"LVB3":{"d":[["South East Pacific","17856","mrgid","",""]]},"LWVHV":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"M3T6M":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION. — Blackites aff. gladius is only known from three records, one in Belgium, one in the Paris Basin and one in the Aquitaine Basin. It rarely co-occurs with Blackites inflatus in the Isnes quarry in SW Belgium, where its presence seems to be restricted to the top of the Brussel Sand Formation. A few specimens have been identified in the Donzacq Marl (upper NP 14) at Saint-Geoursd’Auribat (Aquitaine Basin) (Lin et al. 2017) and in the upper part of the ‘ Glauconie Grossière s. s. ’ at Margival (Paris Basin, sample 3 in Steurbaut 1988), where it also co-occurs with B. inflatus. B. aff. gladius seems to indicate late Biochron NP 14, also known as Biochon NP 14 b (sensu Berggren et al. 1995). It has not been recorded at the Mont-des-Récollets because of major erosion of the top of the Brussel Sand Formation in N France.","","text","",""]]},"MD8ZT":{"d":[["Distribution. E: Azerbaijan, Georgia, Greece (Samos). A: Iran, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Syria, Turkey (Cate 2007).","","text","",""]]},"ML3K":{"d":[["Australia (New South Wales)","","text","",""]]},"MSDS":{"d":[["Oriental(Thailand)","","text","",""]]},"N6THW":{"d":[["Distribution in Iran. Mazandaran (Abe Garm, Damavand Mt.) (Platia & Kakiopoulos 2015). General distribution. Endemic to Iran (Platia & Kakiopoulos 2015).","","text","",""]]},"NPPBG":{"d":[["Middle America","","text","",""],["North America","","text","",""]]},"NWJXP":{"d":[["","FRA","tdwg","",""],["","GRB","tdwg","",""],["","IRE","tdwg","",""],["","SPA","tdwg","",""]]},"P6LQ4":{"d":[["Distribution. Oriental: India (Kerala).","","text","",""]]},"PCDYG":{"d":[["Distribution range of species. from Afghanistan across Himalayas to S. - W. China. Distribution range of subspecies. eastern Afghanistan (first record), N. Pakistan and N. - W. India.","","text","",""]]},"PCSZW":{"d